    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d459">

                <pb facs="0535" n="433" sameAs="frus:frus1933v03/pg433"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.94/845: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Japan
                        (Grew)</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-10-14T15:00:00-05:00">October 14, 1933—3
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>96. Department’s 89, October 6, 5 p.m.,<anchor n="60" xml:id="d459-f1"/>
                    [paragraph] 1. An officer of the Department has spoken with the Japanese
                    Ambassador on the subject of the mooted good will mission, in discouragement
                    thereof. The Ambassador states that he has not been informed or interrogated <pb
                        facs="0536" n="434" xml:id="pg434"/> by his Foreign Office with regard to
                    this project, but that he shares the view that such mission would serve no
                    useful purpose and if interrogated would advise to that effect.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
